+   adds the Active Storage tables. If upgrading from a CarrierWave-only release,
+   route all signed blob requests to proxy-capable web processes before any
+   process publishes Active Storage URLs (e.g. use a blue/green switch). Smoke
+   test both an unchanged profile and a new upload without signing in.
+3. **After deploying all web and worker processes**, run `bin/rails profile_images:copy`
+   in the production Rails environment with access to both stores. It copies
+   the original stored bytes in batches, without reprocessing or altering the
+   source. Each attachment is published only after its upload completes. A
+   concurrent profile edit wins. Do not keep running legacy writers. After
+   copying, the task refreshes legacy avatar URLs in the article snapshots
+   used by feeds, in batches without resaving the articles. This pass also
+   runs on retry if the attachments are already present.
+4. Rerun the same command after an interruption. Already attached records are
+   skipped; successful copies keep the same blob and URL. Errors (including
+   missing files) report the owner type and ID and make the task exit nonzero
+   after processing the other records. Repair the source or storage access and
+   retry. A hard kill during transfer can leave an **unattached** blob, not a
+   broken profile; use normal aged-unattached-blob cleanup, not a purge of all
+   unattached blobs while uploads are in flight.
+5. Verify that a repeat run succeeds with zero images copied and that the URLs
+   on previously legacy-only users and organizations serve the expected bytes.
+   No global read switch is needed: at this point all stored profile images
+   resolve to Active Storage.
 
-Do not drop the columns, remove old files, or roll back the tables after writes
-start. A pre-Active Storage binary cannot serve attachment-only images; keep the
-reader and proxy route in any rollback release. Backfill and retirement of the
-legacy store are separate deploys.
+Do not drop the columns, delete legacy objects, or turn off their public URLs:
+previously rendered pages, historical notifications, search documents, emails,
+CDNs and external clients can still hold those exact URLs. Cached URLs remain
+valid and newly generated image URLs use Active Storage. If using an external
+search index, use its normal reindex operation to refresh previously indexed
+URLs. Retirement of the legacy profile reader requires a separate audited deploy.
+Any rollback after writes start must keep the Active Storage tables, reader,
+storage and proxy route; a CarrierWave-only binary cannot serve attachment-only
+images.
diff --git a/lib/tasks/profile_images.rake b/lib/tasks/profile_images.rake
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cd4fdbf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/tasks/profile_images.rake
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+namespace :profile_images do
+  desc "Copy remaining user and organization CarrierWave profile images into Active Storage"
+  task copy: :environment do
+    failures = 0
+    [User, Organization].each do |model|
+      copied = 0
+      model.in_batches(of: 500) do |batch|
+        remaining = batch.where.not(profile_image: [nil, ""]).where.missing(:profile_image_file_attachment)
+        remaining.select(:id, :profile_image).preload(:profile_image_file_attachment).each do |owner|
+          copied += 1 if Images::CopyProfileImage.call(owner)
+        rescue StandardError => e
+          failures += 1
+          warn "Failed to copy #{model.name} id=#{owner.id} (#{e.class})"
+        end
+      end
+      puts "#{model.name}: #{copied} profile images copied"
+    end
+
+    puts "Refreshing cached article profile image URLs"
+    Articles::RefreshProfileImageUrls.call
+    raise "#{failures} failed profile image copies; correct the errors and rerun" if failures.positive?
+  end
+end
